      "writtenOn": "2022-12-09T16:55:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e ... for types defined outside of the crate\n\nRight, `AvbFooter` comes from the bindgen, I had missed that ...\n\nBut what about implementing a `Footer` that `repr(transparent)` an `AvbFooter` so that we can add methods and `impl` traits for it, making a proper Rust struct?\n\nWe would then have the constructor `avb::Footer::from_image()` (`std`-only) that would\n```\nlet mut bytes \u003d [0; size_of::\u003cAvbFooter\u003e()];\nimage.read_exact(\u0026mut bytes).map_err(...)?;\nbytes.try_into()\n```\nand the `impl TryFrom\u003c...\u003e` wrapping `avb_footer_validate_and_byteswap`.",
      "parentUuid": "4e5f2a21_94aeb6e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "8794ed860bf7d10c9bc306bc531f7c6a8f84d835",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
