      "writtenOn": "2022-12-12T15:25:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I added `Footer` and `try_from(bytes)` for now.\n\nGreat!\n\nBTW, (`Try`)`From` typically converts \"by value\" so this should take the array directly instead of `TryFrom\u003c\u0026[...` (as I suggested above).\n\nThe point is was making in [another comment](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2337745/comment/09e64a75_32a5889e/) was that the convoluted `unsafe{MaybeUninit+copy_nonoverlapping}` you currently have in `try_from` could then be replaced by a trivial and safe cloning in the caller:\n\n```\nOk(Footer::TryFrom(raw_footer.clone()).ok())\n```\n\n\u003e maybe we need to add another VbImageVerificationError here\n\nYes, returning `VbMetaImageVerificationError::InvalidFooter` makes sense, even if we ignore it (`.ok()`) for now. But I agree that plumbing it through can be kept as a TODO.",
      "parentUuid": "6b6984bf_80e34d0e",
